# Server TLS ExpectedServerName binding — STOP closeout

The task stopped at §9 before functional changes: the existing channel TLS/security models do not supply an approved ExpectedServerName with revision, lifetime and issuer binding. A security reference, candidate name or certificate SAN cannot fill that authority gap. See [source evidence and minimal handoff](source-proof-and-handoff.md) and [focal proposal](SOURCE-DECISION-PROPOSED.md). The proposal is NOT ACCEPTED.

